{
  "class": "BlockEntityDataPacket",
  "module": "server/play/block_entity_data_packet",
  "module_docs": [
    "Port of",
    "`net.minestom.server.network.packet.server.play.BlockEntityDataPacket`.",
    "",
    "Java's `BlockEntityType` is a `StaticProtocolObject` written as a var int",
    "protocol id; the `instance` block registry is not ported, so the port",
    "carries the id itself. Java's `data` is an adventure `CompoundBinaryTag`;",
    "the port uses the `nbt` module's [`CompoundBinaryTag`], and an absent tag is",
    "written as a bare `TAG_End` exactly as Java does.",
    "",
    "Java's deprecated `(Point, int action, CompoundBinaryTag)` constructor is",
    "replaced by [`BlockEntityDataPacket::from_action`], which panics where",
    "Java's `Objects.requireNonNull(BlockEntityType.fromId(action), \u2026)` throws."
  ],
  "struct": {
    "docs": [
      "Java: `record BlockEntityDataPacket(Point blockPosition, BlockEntityType type,",
      "@Nullable CompoundBinaryTag data) implements ServerPacket.Play`.",
      "",
      "Java's `blockPosition` is a `Point`; the port carries the decoded",
      "[`CoordVec`], as [`BLOCK_POSITION`] reads it back."
    ],
    "derives": [
      "Clone",
      "Debug",
      "PartialEq"
    ],
    "form": "braced"
  },
  "fields": [
    {
